 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385845 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}\\,0 & \\,1 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}\\,0 & \\,1 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\,0 & \\,1 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -9)(\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385846 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bd61e26a-f154-5f32-82ad-e5ead117f18e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759